INT. THRONE ROOM OF THE GLASS KING - NIGHT

A hall of translucent pillars lit from within by drifting blue flame. Snow falls indoors from a ceiling that has no ceiling. At the far end, a crystalline throne.

KING ORIVEN THE CLEAR, 60s, crowned in frost, sits motionless upon it. At his right stands his sorceress sister LADY MYRRHEN, 50s, hooded. To his left, the captain of his guard, SER BRANDOLF GRAYMANE, 40s, in silver plate. Before the throne, kneeling on cold stone, are three travelers: a tattooed dwarf-smith named GRIMBOLD STONEHAND, a young archer with a green scarf named THISTLE, and a robed monk named BROTHER ANSELM.

Snowflakes catch on their shoulders.

KING ORIVEN
Rise.

They rise. Thistle stumbles. Grimbold steadies her.

KING ORIVEN (CONT'D)
You carry the Ember.

GRIMBOLD
We carry nothing.

THISTLE
We carry a letter.

BROTHER ANSELM
We carry a request.

LADY MYRRHEN
(simultaneously)
They carry the Ember.

^SER BRANDOLF
They carry a lie.

King Oriven raises one hand. Silence. A flake lands on his open palm and does not melt.

KING ORIVEN
Show me the letter.

Thistle fumbles at her satchel. Grimbold holds up his hand to stop her.

GRIMBOLD
It's not for you.

SER BRANDOLF
You speak to a king.

GRIMBOLD
I speak to a man with a very cold hall.

THISTLE
Grimbold.

BROTHER ANSELM
Peace, friends. Majesty, the letter is for the Queen of the Ash Court.

LADY MYRRHEN
There is no Queen of the Ash Court.

BROTHER ANSELM
There was.

SER BRANDOLF
The Ash Court burned.

THISTLE
That's why we need her.

KING ORIVEN
(softly)
Enough.

Everyone stops. He stands, slowly, his crown ringing like a struck bell. He descends one step, then another. He stops in front of Thistle and looks into her scarf, her face, her quiver.

KING ORIVEN (CONT'D)
Child. Who gave you that scarf?

THISTLE
My mother.

KING ORIVEN
And her name?

THISTLE
Ashlyn.

Lady Myrrhen's hood falls back. Ser Brandolf's hand lowers from his sword. King Oriven closes his eyes.

KING ORIVEN (CONT'D)
Then the letter is for me.
